{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Measured on a copy of the live store (9,731 entries), tracemalloc peak during the call, each read in its own process, outputs saved as JSON from origin/main 3b80ff04452 (before) and from the change (after) and compared for equality. All 11 equal.\n- search full (query 'memory', 253 rows): 348.9 -> 66.4 MB, equal\n- search lean: 348.7 -> 66.4 MB, equal\n- recent_session_logs (limit 5): 284.4 -> 10.8 MB, equal\n- binding drift (audit_binding_drift): 328.7 -> 66.4 MB, equal (9 drift classes)\n- validate (normalize_issues over _raw_tickets, 213 issues): 284.4 -> 12.6 MB, equal\n- validate_state full report: 284.4 -> 12.3 MB, equal\n- ticket_deps graph-cache miss (_compute_dep_graph on this ticket): 284.5 -> 44.4 MB, equal\n- list --status=open full body: 284.4 -> 11.7 MB, equal (92)\n- list --status=open lean (CLI shape): 64.2 -> 11.0 MB, equal\n- list open + blocking_state=unblocked full body: 284.4 -> 47.9 MB, equal (69)\n- list open + blocking_state=unblocked lean: 64.9 -> 46.4 MB, equal; the remainder is find_ready_tickets' lean pass, unchanged by design.\nThe remaining 66.4 MB in search and drift is the binding store: binding_jira_key_map alone peaks at 66.4 MB parsing the 22 MB bindings.json. That load predates this change; filed separately. The observation's 106.6 MB for the blocking_state list was not reproduced: the CLI-shaped lean read measured 64.9 MB here."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793306721381602001,"uuid":"c0b30d8d-88ba-4bb3-9996-84ca796f77f8"}